Calendar-based is the classic OpenTTD experience, with a year consisting of 12 months, and each month having 28-31 days.

In Wallclock-based time, cargo production and financials are instead based on one-minute increments, which is about as long as a 30 day month takes in Calendar-based mode. These are grouped into 12-minute periods, equivalent to a year in Calendar-based mode.

In either mode there is always a classic calendar, which is used for introduction dates of vehicles, houses, and other infrastructureCalendar	WallclockMinutes per year: ÓÄÆ¡~Choose the number of minutes in a calendar year. The default is 12 minutes. Set to 0 to stop calendar time from changing. Increasing the length of the calendar year slows down the introduction of vehicles, houses, and other infrastructure. It does not affect vehicle speed or economic simulation, except for inflation. This setting is only available when using wallclock timekeepingÓÄ∑0 (calendar time frozen) Scale town cargo production: ÓÄÆ6Scale the cargo production of towns by this percentage$Scale industry cargo production: ÓÄÆ;Scale the cargo production of industries by this percentageÓÄ∑%'Autorenew vehicle when it gets old: ÓÄÆsWhen enabled, a vehicle nearing its end of life gets automatically replaced when the renew conditions are fulfilled)Autorenew when vehicle is ÓÄÆ maximum ageBRelative age when a vehicle should be considered for auto-renewingÓÄµ monthÓÄº␀␀␀s beforeÓÄµ monthÓÄº␀␀␀s after-Autorenew minimum needed money for renew: ÓÄÆ^Minimal amount of money that must remain in the bank before considering auto-renewing vehiclesDuration of error message: ÓÄÆ™Duration for displaying error messages in a red window. Note that some (critical) error messages are not closed automatically after this time, but must be closed manuallyShow tooltips: ÓÄÆØDelay before tooltips are displayed when hovering the mouse over some interface element. Alternatively tooltips are bound to the right mouse button when this value is set to 0"Hover for ÓÄµ millisecondÓÄº␀␀␀sRight click0Show town population in the town name label: ÓÄÆ9Display the population of towns in their label on the map!Thickness of lines in graphs: ÓÄÆéWidth of the line in the graphs. A thin line is more precisely readable, a thicker line is easier to see and colours are easier to distinguish7Show the NewGRF's name in the build v